{"qid":"Q232","names":["Kazakhstan"],"title":"Kazakhstan","endonym":{"native":"Қазақстан","lang":"kk"},"capsule":"The Republic of Kazakhstan declared independence from the Soviet Union on 16 December 1991 (the last Soviet republic to do so) and was formally recognized internationally after the USSR's dissolution on 25 December 1991. The world's largest landlocked country by area, Kazakhstan holds major hydrocarbon reserves and has pursued a multi-vector foreign policy under Nursultan Nazarbayev (president 1991–2019) and his successor Kassym-Jomart Tokayev. Widespread protests in January 2022 (triggered by fuel price increases) led to a military crackdown with CSTO assistance and Nazarbayev's formal removal from remaining constitutional offices.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. International borders are formally delimited and well-documented, though the Caspian Sea boundary remains subject to an unresolved legal framework among littoral states.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kazakhstan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazakhstan"},{"label":"Britannica: Kazakhstan","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Kazakhstan"},{"label":"Britannica: Nursultan Nazarbayev","url":"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Nursultan-Nazarbayev"}],"britannica":"place/Kazakhstan","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kazakhstan","rulers":[{"qid":"Q1963481","name":"Sergey Tereshchenko","start":1991,"end":1994,"image":"Sergey Tereshchenko (2016-04-01).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sergey%20Tereshchenko%20(2016-04-01).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 3.0","artist":"